#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:107
msgid "Basics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:109
msgid ""
"A ROS workspace is a directory with a particular structure. Commonly there "
"is a ``src`` subdirectory. Inside that subdirectory is where the source code "
"of ROS packages will be located. Typically the directory starts otherwise "
"empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:114
msgid ""
"colcon performs out-of-source builds. By default it will create the "
"following directories as peers of the ``src`` directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:117
msgid ""
"The ``build`` directory will be where intermediate files are stored. For "
"each package a subfolder will be created in which e.g. CMake is being "
"invoked."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:119
msgid ""
"The ``install`` directory is where each package will be installed to. By "
"default each package will be installed into a separate subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:121
msgid ""
"The ``log`` directory contains various logging information about each colcon "
"invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:123
msgid "Compared to catkin there is no ``devel`` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:126
msgid "Create a workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:128
