#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:163
msgid "Add some sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:165
msgid ""
"Let's clone the `examples <https://github.com/ros2/examples>`__ repository "
"into the ``src`` directory of the workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:167
msgid "$ git clone https://github.com/ros2/examples src/examples -b rolling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:171
msgid "Now the workspace should have the source code to the ROS 2 examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:173
msgid ""
".\n"
"└── src\n"
"    └── examples\n"
"        ├── CONTRIBUTING.md\n"
"        ├── LICENSE\n"
"        ├── rclcpp\n"
"        ├── rclpy\n"
"        └── README.md\n"
"\n"
"4 directories, 3 files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:187
msgid "Source an underlay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:189
msgid ""
"It is important that we have sourced the environment for an existing ROS 2 "
"installation that will provide our workspace with the necessary build "
"dependencies for the example packages. This is achieved by sourcing the "
"setup script provided by a binary installation or a source installation, i."
"e. another colcon workspace (see :doc:`Installation <../../../Get-Started/"
"Installation>`). We call this environment an **underlay**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:193
msgid ""
"Our workspace, ``ros2_ws``, will be an **overlay** on top of the existing "
"ROS 2 installation. In general, it is recommended to use an overlay when you "
"plan to iterate on a small number of packages, rather than putting all of "
"your packages into the same workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:197
msgid "Build the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:201
msgid ""
"To build packages on Windows you need to be in a Visual Studio environment, "
"see :ref:`Building the ROS 2 Code <windows-dev-build-ros2>` for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:203
msgid ""
"In the root of the workspace, run ``colcon build``. Since build types such "
"as ``ament_cmake`` do not support the concept of the ``devel`` space and "
"require the package to be installed, colcon supports the option ``--symlink-"
"install``. This allows the installed files to be changed by changing the "
"files in the ``source`` space (e.g. Python files or other non-compiled "
"resources) for faster iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:211
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:217
msgid "$ colcon build --symlink-install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:223
msgid "$ colcon build --merge-install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:227
msgid ""
"Windows doesn't allow long paths, so ``merge-install`` will combine all the "
"paths into the ``install`` directory. On Windows, you need special "
"permissions to create symbolic links, so ``--symlink-install`` is not used "
"by default. To use it, you need to run the command as administrator or "
"enable developer mode in system settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:233
msgid ""
"Running ``colcon build`` may freeze the screen and mouse of systems that are "
"CPU-, RAM- and I/O-limited (e.g., Raspberry Pi), so it might be useful to "
"use the ``--executor sequential`` argument to build the packages one by one "
"instead of using parallelism. See the `colcon documentation <https://colcon."
"readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/executor-arguments.html>`_ for more "
"arguments as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:236
msgid ""
"After the build is finished, we should see the ``build``, ``install``, and "
"``log`` directories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:238
msgid ""
".\n"
"├── build\n"
"├── install\n"
"├── log\n"
"└── src\n"
"\n"
"4 directories, 0 files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:251
msgid "Run tests"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:253
msgid "To run tests for the packages we just built, run the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:259
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:265
msgid "$ colcon test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:271
msgid ""
"Remember to use a ``x64 Native Tools Command Prompt for VS 2019`` for "
"executing the following command, as we are going to build a workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:273
msgid "$ colcon test --merge-install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:277
msgid ""
"You also need to specify ``--merge-install`` here since we used it for "
"building above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:282
msgid "Source the environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:284
msgid ""
"When colcon has completed building successfully, the output will be in the "
"``install`` directory. Before you can use any of the installed executables "
"or libraries, you will need to add them to your path and library paths. "
"colcon will have generated bash/bat files in the ``install`` directory to "
"help set up the environment. These files will add all of the required "
"elements to your path and library paths as well as provide any bash or shell "
"commands exported by packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:293
msgid "$ source install/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:299
msgid "$ . install/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:305
msgid "In a Windows command line interface:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:307
msgid "$ call install\\setup.bat"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:311
msgid "Or with Powershell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:313
msgid "$ install\\setup.ps1"
msgstr ""

