msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:336
msgid "Create your own package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:338
msgid ""
"colcon uses the ``package.xml`` specification defined in `REP 149 <https://"
"reps.openrobotics.org/rep-0149/>`__ (`format 2 <https://reps.openrobotics."
"org/rep-0140/>`__ is also supported)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:340
msgid ""
"colcon supports multiple build types. The recommended build types are "
"``ament_cmake`` and ``ament_python``. Also supported are pure ``cmake`` "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:344
msgid ""
"An example of an ``ament_python`` build is the `ament_index_python package "
"<https://github.com/ament/ament_index/tree/rolling/ament_index_python>`__ , "
"where the setup.py is the primary entry point for building."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:346
msgid ""
"A package such as `demo_nodes_cpp <https://github.com/ros2/demos/tree/"
"rolling/demo_nodes_cpp>`__ uses the ``ament_cmake`` build type, and uses "
"CMake as the build tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:348
msgid ""
"For convenience, you can use the tool ``ros2 pkg create`` to create a new "
"package based on a template. A full description of creating a package and "
"how to use ``ros2 pkg create`` is in the upcoming tutorial :doc:`create a "
"package <Creating-Your-First-ROS2-Package>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:351
msgid ""
"For ``catkin`` users, this is the equivalent of ``catkin_create_package``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:354
msgid "Setup ``colcon_cd``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:356
msgid ""
"The command ``colcon_cd`` allows you to quickly change the current working "
"directory of your shell to the directory of a package. As an example "
"``colcon_cd some_ros_package`` would quickly bring you to the directory ``~/"
"ros2_ws/src/some_ros_package``. To set up ``colcon_cd`` you need to run the "
"following commands to modify your shell startup script:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:364
msgid ""
"$ echo \"source /etc/profile.d/colcon_cd.sh\" >> ~/.bashrc\n"
"$ echo \"export _colcon_cd_root=/opt/ros/rolling/\" >> ~/.bashrc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:371
msgid ""
"$ echo \"source /usr/local/share/colcon_cd/function/colcon_cd.sh\" >> ~/."
"bashrc\n"
"$ echo \"export _colcon_cd_root=~/ros2_install\" >> ~/.bashrc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:378
msgid "Not yet available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:380
msgid ""
"Depending on the way you installed ``colcon_cd`` and where your workspace "
"is, the instructions above may vary, please refer to `the documentation "
"<https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/user/installation.html#quick-"
"directory-changes>`__ for more details. To undo this in Linux and macOS, "
"locate your system's shell startup script and remove the appended source and "
"export commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:384
msgid "Setup ``colcon`` tab completion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:386
msgid ""
"The ``colcon`` command supports command completion for bash and bash-like "
"shells. The ``colcon-argcomplete`` package must be installed, and `some "
"setup may be required <https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/user/"
"installation.html#enable-completion>`__ to make it work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:390
msgid "Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:392
msgid ""
"If you do not want to build a specific package, then place an empty file "
"named ``COLCON_IGNORE`` in the directory and it will not be indexed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:394
msgid ""
"If you want to avoid configuring and building tests in CMake packages you "
"can pass: ``--cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:396
msgid "If you want to run a single particular test from a package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:398
msgid ""
"$ colcon test --packages-select YOUR_PKG_NAME --ctest-args -R "
"YOUR_TEST_IN_PKG"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:403
msgid "Setup ``colcon`` mixins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:405
msgid ""
"Various command line options are tedious to write and/or difficult to "
"remember."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:407
msgid "For example, to change the CMake build type to debug, you normally use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:409
msgid "$ colcon build --cmake-args -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:413
msgid ""
"To make common command line options easier to invoke this repository makes "
"these \"shortcuts\" available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:415
msgid "To install the default colcon mixins, run the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:417
msgid ""
"$ colcon mixin add default https://raw.githubusercontent.com/colcon/colcon-"
"mixin-repository/master/index.yaml\n"
"$ colcon mixin update default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:422
msgid "Then, try out using the ``debug`` mixin:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:424
msgid "$ colcon build --mixin debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/client-libraries/Working-with-Client-Libraries/Colcon-Tutorial.rst:428
msgid ""
"For more details, see  the `colcon mixin repository <https://github.com/"
"colcon/colcon-mixin-repository>`__."
msgstr ""
